<title>RUSSIA: Russian 203-day T-bill yields 36.49 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian 203-day T-bill yields 36.49 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised average yield on an issue of 203-day GKO discount Treasury bills (series 22079) was 36.49 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast the average yield would be 36.00-36.98 percent.</p>
<p>Series 22075 bills, maturing on October 29, 1997, the closest maturity date to the new issue, closed at 82.77 to yield 36.01 percent on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>The full results of the T-bill auction:</p>
<p>    Series number			  22079</p>
<p>    Issue volume			    7.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations			   1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)			 10.83 trln</p>
<p>    Bids (cash)			     8.87 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)			  6.49 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds				  5.39 trln</p>
<p>    Average price			  83.13 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price		82.94 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield			  36.49 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield	     36.98 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor				    203 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date			  Oct 22, 1997</p>
<p>On Wednesday the Finance Ministry is also auctioning four trillion roubles of 728-day OFZ interest-bearing government bonds (series 24011) and will repay about 6.92 trillion roubles in a maturing issue of six month T-bills (series 23047).</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
